## Scope

- preserve the reviewed feature-source and published-snapshot fixture isolation;
- add one canonical recovery contract pinned to exact immutable v0.6.2, PR #52, the original main validation, every job in the original Prepare Release run, the failed required check, branch-protection identity, and the retained successful preflight artifact;
- keep ordinary ledger validation authoritative, with a fail-closed exception only for PR #53 and its direct activation merge;
- run the complete reusable source suite against exact v0.6.2, overlaying only the two reviewed fixture files in the fast lane;
- attest release, harness, activation, workflow, lane, and artifact identities separately;
- identify the activation PR through the commit association, then fetch full PR detail before verifying author and merger identity;
- after every required recovery lane passes, publish a GitHub Actions check named `Source test suite / Required source checks` on exact immutable PR #52 head;
- handle GitHub's per-suite `filter=latest` results without discarding historical failures: bind the exact new REST ID, GraphQL node, suite, completion time, run/attempt, artifact, and lane evidence; require that exact `CheckRun` to remain current in its suite and that GitHub reports it required for PR #52; reject missing, wrong-app, failed, stale, duplicate, pending, conflicting, or superseding evidence;
- extend approval authorization to repeat the exact check-node, branch-protection, PR-state, historical-failure, lane, and evidence verification after PR #52 merges;
- stage the recovery-aware verifier from that merge before the deploy workflow checks the old immutable release code;
- hold automatic v0.6.3 creation until this one-time recovery is retired after v0.6.2 is confirmed in production.

No immutable release, application, receiver, Nginx configuration, Discord setting, branch protection, or VPS state is changed. This PR does not merge PR #52, activate recovery, publish a production approval marker, or deploy. Broader restructuring remains deferred.

## Exact identities

- Recovery source/main base: `4f98e7cb559ee1a9b269ea1f94938678d2dac4df`
- Final PR #53 head: `a8aaf10e03c35a5510f0a7e03a92d4f19e8be0e8`
- Immutable v0.6.2 / PR #52 head: `6074b965cbd2e6ab2630cd539ee455b8d419aef6`
- v0.6.2 tree: `cfcd1f21903d3609aef0bbd7b61950be5fef2aa5`
- v0.6.2 `RELEASE.json`: `c9cf79d34c8b3f90556e405f338ee4c1e7818d9c686f0462eec7dca201b784f4`
- Original main validation: run `34297290478`, attempt 1
- Original Prepare Release/preflight: run `34297562022`, attempt 1
- Retained preflight artifact: `10083806725`, digest `sha256:d527be28e5f79972835cd2d12c92e6ce98f4c9f77f081e872df76908c6ca0510`
- Historical failed required check: run `34297801831`, check `102298823162`, suite `92911719969`
- Protected required context/app: `Source test suite / Required source checks`, GitHub Actions app `15368`

## Final validation

- Hosted Validate PR `34416936121`: all eight lanes passed on the exact final head, including authoritative required-source check `102684563322`. This includes Linux fast/unit/migration/JavaScript, MariaDB/Redis/Celery/fake ESI integration, previous-schema upgrade and backup restoration, browser, permission, release-ledger, and change-fragment coverage.
- Preview UI `34416935856`: passed on the exact final head. Manifest artifact `10129527081` (`sha256:943b989ae17b2bfc8a49cc24b841658047f6109238620aa9888559439d7d51bd`) and evidence artifact `10129526658` (`sha256:e5b98688d63820e820e1b30bf1d2ff2cf49f6924b9928c87d7c1d49404258172`) expire on 12 September. Their manifests are byte-identical; all 128 declared PNGs passed the bounded validator across five themes and both viewports, with synthetic-only data, internal-only networking, and a nonempty Playwright report.
- Local: 91 focused recovery/configuration/workflow/approval tests passed; the complete coordinated recovery-to-authorization rehearsal passed; Ruff, Python compilation, supply-chain verification, and `git diff --check` passed. The repository fast script passed all 103 platform tests; its deploy discovery completed 196 tests with 12 skips before the known Windows-host absence of POSIX `fcntl`. Hosted Linux validation above passed that authoritative deploy coverage.
- The exact GraphQL operation was exercised read-only against historical PR #52 check `102298823162`: GitHub returned the pinned release SHA, suite `92911719969`, PR state `OPEN`, and `isRequired: true`. The future recovery check's suite/node cannot be observed before activation and must be captured and verified by the reviewed workflow.
- Trusted readiness is requested only after this final body update. The final bot-authored canonical readiness pointer—not an older run named here—is authoritative for the exact head.

## Review and activation

The exact ordered Work activation procedure is in `ops/release/README.md` under **One-time published-v0.6.2 validation recovery**. This PR only prepares and tests that mechanism. The new required check on immutable PR #52 cannot and must not be created before Work reviews and merges this activation PR, confirms activation-main CI and the v0.6.3 hold, and dispatches the one-time recovery workflow at attempt 1.

That workflow must retain historical failure `102298823162`, publish the new GitHub Actions result on exact release SHA `6074b965cbd2e6ab2630cd539ee455b8d419aef6`, capture its actual check node/suite, prove that exact check is required for PR #52, reject conflicting or superseding evidence, and publish recovery readiness only afterward. Work must inspect that live evidence before presenting the separate production approval to Anthony. If any pinned identity or the retained preflight changes or expires, stop rather than bypassing the gate.

